// `bxrig setup boot` / `setup undo boot` / `setup boot status`: the BxRig boot splash (Plymouth). The laptop fades in over a soft
// green-to-cyan glow, five dots pulse while the system starts, and an encrypted disk asks for its password on the same screen.
// What `setup boot --yes` does, each step shown in the plan first:
//   1. installs plymouth when missing (pacman)
//   2. puts the theme in /usr/share/plymouth/themes/bxrig (bxrig.plymouth, bxrig.script, logo.png, glow.png, dot.png)
//   3. adds the plymouth hook to HOOKS in /etc/mkinitcpio.conf when it is not there (after systemd or udev; a backup first:
//      /etc/mkinitcpio.conf.bxrig-backup)
//   4. `plymouth-set-default-theme -R bxrig` (sets it and rebuilds the initramfs)
// The splash shows only when the kernel command line has `splash` (and usually `quiet`). BxRig does not edit boot loaders; the plan
// says where to add it for the one it finds (Limine, GRUB, systemd-boot).
// Undo sets the theme that was there before (saved in ~/.local/state/bxrig/setup-boot.json), rebuilds, removes the theme folder;
// the hook stays (it is harmless and other themes need it).
// Test overrides: BXRIG_PLYMOUTH_DIR, BXRIG_MKINITCPIO, BXRIG_CMDLINE, BXRIG_BOOT_DIR.
// Exit: 0 done, 2 plan without --yes, 4 precondition (root, not Arch), 5 pacman, 6 a step failed.
class BootSplash {
	function init( cli, runner = "" ) {
		variables.cli = arguments.cli;
		variables.environ = new bxrig.util.Env();
		variables.inst = new bxrig.Installer( arguments.runner );
		variables.proc = variables.inst.proc();
		variables.pacman = new bxrig.util.Pacman( variables.proc );
		variables.out = new bxrig.util.Out( variables.cli, "setup boot" );
		return this;
	}

	function themesDir() { return variables.environ.get( "BXRIG_PLYMOUTH_DIR", "/usr/share/plymouth/themes" ); }
	function themeDir() { return themesDir() & "/bxrig"; }
	function mkinitcpio() { return variables.environ.get( "BXRIG_MKINITCPIO", "/etc/mkinitcpio.conf" ); }
	function cmdline() {
		var f = variables.environ.get( "BXRIG_CMDLINE", "/proc/cmdline" );
		return fileExists( f ) ? trim( fileRead( f ) ) : "";
	}
	function bootDir() { return variables.environ.get( "BXRIG_BOOT_DIR", "/boot" ); }
	function stateFile() { return new bxrig.ConfigService().stateDir() & "/setup-boot.json"; }

	// The HOOKS line has plymouth.
	function hasHook() {
		if ( !fileExists( mkinitcpio() ) ) return false;
		for ( var line in listToArray( fileRead( mkinitcpio() ), chr( 10 ) ) ) {
			if ( left( trim( line ), 6 ) == "HOOKS=" ) return reFindNoCase( "[( ]plymouth[ )]", line ) > 0;
		}
		return false;
	}
	function hasSplash() { return listFind( cmdline(), "splash", " " ) > 0; }
	function currentTheme() {
		var r = variables.proc.exec( [ "plymouth-set-default-theme" ], 10 );
		return r.exitCode == 0 ? trim( r.output ) : "";
	}
	// Where to add `splash`, for the boot loader found.
	function splashHint() {
		var b = bootDir();
		if ( fileExists( b & "/limine.conf" ) || fileExists( b & "/limine/limine.conf" ) || fileExists( "/etc/default/limine" ) )
			return "Limine: add `quiet splash` to KERNEL_CMDLINE in /etc/default/limine (CachyOS), or to the cmdline: lines of limine.conf, then reboot";
		if ( fileExists( "/etc/default/grub" ) ) return "GRUB: add `quiet splash` to GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX_DEFAULT in /etc/default/grub, then `sudo grub-mkconfig -o /boot/grub/grub.cfg`";
		if ( directoryExists( b & "/loader/entries" ) ) return "systemd-boot: add `quiet splash` to the options line of your entry in " & b & "/loader/entries/, then reboot";
		return "add `quiet splash` to your kernel command line, then reboot";
	}

	// The theme files written to a staging folder (copied into place with sudo by the plan).
	function stage( dir ) {
		directoryCreate( arguments.dir, true, true );
		var td = new bxrig.TemplateData();
		fileWrite( arguments.dir & "/bxrig.plymouth", td.text( "plymouth/bxrig.plymouth" ) );
		fileWrite( arguments.dir & "/bxrig.script", td.text( "plymouth/bxrig.script" ) );
		var assets = new bxrig.Assets( variables.cli, variables.inst.runner() );
		for ( var img in [ "logo.png", "glow.png", "dot.png" ] ) assets.decode( "plymouth/" & img, arguments.dir & "/" & img );
	}

	// sed: on the HOOKS= line without plymouth, put plymouth after systemd, else after udev (MatchBox literals drop backslashes: chr( 92 ))
	function hookSed() {
		var b = chr( 92 );
		return "/^HOOKS=/{/plymouth/!{s/" & b & "b(systemd)" & b & "b/" & b & "1 plymouth/;t;s/" & b & "b(udev)" & b & "b/" & b & "1 plymouth/}}";
	}

	function plan( staging ) {
		var p = { steps: [], notes: [], errors: [] };
		if ( variables.proc.isRoot() ) p.errors.append( "Run as a regular user; sudo is used for the steps that need it" );
		if ( !variables.proc.has( "pacman" ) ) p.errors.append( "The boot splash setup needs Arch Linux or CachyOS (pacman and mkinitcpio)" );
		if ( p.errors.len() ) return p;
		if ( !variables.pacman.isInstalled( "plymouth" ) ) p.steps.append( { id: "package", title: "install plymouth", commands: [ variables.pacman.installArgv( [ "plymouth" ], false ) ] } );
		p.steps.append( { id: "theme", title: "put the BxRig theme in " & themeDir(), stage: true,
			commands: [ [ "sudo", "install", "-d", "-m", "755", themeDir() ], [ "sudo", "sh", "-c", 'cp -f "$1"/* "$2"/ && chmod 644 "$2"/*', "_", arguments.staging, themeDir() ] ] } );
		if ( !hasHook() ) {
			if ( !fileExists( mkinitcpio() ) ) p.notes.append( "No " & mkinitcpio() & ": add the plymouth hook to your initramfs yourself" );
			else p.steps.append( { id: "hook", title: "add the plymouth hook to HOOKS in " & mkinitcpio() & " (backup: " & mkinitcpio() & ".bxrig-backup)",
				commands: [ [ "sudo", "cp", "-n", mkinitcpio(), mkinitcpio() & ".bxrig-backup" ],
							[ "sudo", "sed", "-i", "-E", hookSed(), mkinitcpio() ] ] } );
		}
		p.steps.append( { id: "default", title: "make bxrig the boot theme and rebuild the initramfs", commands: [ [ "sudo", "plymouth-set-default-theme", "-R", "bxrig" ] ] } );
		if ( !hasSplash() ) p.notes.append( "The splash shows only with `splash` on the kernel command line. " & splashHint() & "." );
		return p;
	}

	function run( verb, yes, dry, asJson ) {
		if ( arguments.verb == "status" ) {
			var d = { installed: directoryExists( themeDir() ), current: currentTheme(), hook: hasHook(), splash: hasSplash() };
			return variables.out.say( "ok", d, arguments.asJson, [ "theme: " & ( d.installed ? "installed" : "not installed" ) & ( len( d.current ) ? " (active: " & d.current & ")" : "" ),
				"plymouth hook: " & ( d.hook ? "yes" : "no" ), "splash on the kernel command line: " & ( d.splash ? "yes" : "no (" & splashHint() & ")" ) ] );
		}
		if ( arguments.verb == "undo" ) return undo( arguments.yes, arguments.dry, arguments.asJson );
		var staging = variables.environ.cache( "boot-splash" );
		var p = plan( staging );
		var data = { steps: p.steps, notes: p.notes, errors: p.errors, done: [], failed: [] };
		if ( p.errors.len() ) return variables.out.say( "precondition", data, arguments.asJson, p.errors.map( function( e ) { return "error: " & e; } ) );
		var lines = [ "Plan: setup boot, " & p.steps.len() & " steps" ];
		for ( var s in p.steps ) { lines.append( "  " & s.id & ": " & s.title ); for ( var c in s.commands ) lines.append( "    " & c.toList( " " ) ); }
		for ( var n in p.notes ) lines.append( "  note: " & n );
		if ( arguments.dry || !arguments.yes ) { lines.append( new bxrig.util.Mutation().footer( arguments.dry ) ); return variables.out.say( arguments.dry ? "ok" : "plan", data, arguments.asJson, lines, arguments.dry ); }
		var before = currentTheme();
		if ( len( before ) && before != "bxrig" ) {
			directoryCreate( getDirectoryFromPath( stateFile() ), true, true );
			fileWrite( stateFile(), jsonSerialize( { previous: before } ) );
		}
		var code = 0;
		for ( var s in p.steps ) {
			if ( s.stage ?: false ) { try { stage( staging ); } catch ( any e ) { data.failed.append( { id: s.id, error: e.message } ); code = 6; break; } }
			var bad = "";
			for ( var c in s.commands ) {
				var r = variables.proc.exec( c, 1800 );
				if ( r.timeout || r.exitCode != 0 ) { bad = "exit " & ( r.timeout ? 124 : r.exitCode ) & ": " & trim( r.output ); break; }
			}
			if ( len( bad ) ) { data.failed.append( { id: s.id, error: bad } ); code = s.id == "package" ? 5 : 6; break; }
			data.done.append( s.id );
		}
		if ( directoryExists( staging ) ) { try { directoryDelete( staging, true ); } catch ( any e ) {} }
		var out = [];
		for ( var d in data.done ) out.append( "Done: " & d );
		for ( var f in data.failed ) out.append( "Failed: " & f.id & " (" & f.error & ")" );
		if ( !data.failed.len() ) for ( var n in p.notes ) out.append( "Note: " & n );
		return variables.out.say( code == 0 ? "ok" : code, data, arguments.asJson, out );
	}

	function undo( yes, dry, asJson ) {
		var prev = "";
		var st = new bxrig.util.Json().read( stateFile() );
		if ( isStruct( st ) ) prev = st.previous ?: "";
		var cmds = [];
		cmds.append( len( prev ) ? [ "sudo", "plymouth-set-default-theme", "-R", prev ] : [ "sudo", "plymouth-set-default-theme", "-r", "-R" ] );
		cmds.append( [ "sudo", "rm", "-rf", themeDir() ] );
		var lines = [ "Plan: setup undo boot", "  " & ( len( prev ) ? "back to the " & prev & " theme" : "back to the default theme" ) & " and remove " & themeDir() ];
		var data = { previous: prev, commands: cmds };
		if ( arguments.dry || !arguments.yes ) { lines.append( new bxrig.util.Mutation().footer( arguments.dry ) ); return variables.out.say( arguments.dry ? "ok" : "plan", data, arguments.asJson, lines, arguments.dry ); }
		for ( var c in cmds ) {
			var r = variables.proc.exec( c, 1800 );
			if ( r.timeout || r.exitCode != 0 ) return variables.out.say( "failed", data, arguments.asJson, [ "error: " & c.toList( " " ) & " failed: " & trim( r.output ) ] );
		}
		if ( fileExists( stateFile() ) ) fileDelete( stateFile() );
		return variables.out.say( "ok", data, arguments.asJson, [ "The boot splash is back to " & ( len( prev ) ? prev : "the default" ) & "." ] );
	}
}
